# Content UI

The shell (topbar, sidebar, drawer) and the inner pages follow the Graphite identity (`DESIGN.md`; spec `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-09-graphite-identity.md`). Inner canvas pages follow the patterns below.

Inner pages live in `.canvas` and use the shared pieces:

- Page title: `.page-head` with one `h1` and an optional `.lede`. Do not repeat the header greeting.
- Section: `.pane` and `.pane-head`. One card style.
- Tabs: `.steps`.
- Workbench: a `.filter-bar` that is a direct child of `.desk`, followed by `.pane`, is one surface. The bar is the head; the pane is the body. Do not give the bar its own card shadow.
- Filters: `.filter-bar` > `.filter-panel`, above the table, never inside the table head. Filters apply as the user changes them.
- Scroll: the shell is `100dvh` with `overflow: hidden`. Workbench lists (`.desk` → `.filter-bar` + `.pane` + `.sheet`) fill the canvas and **the sheet scrolls**. Multi-block pages (`.desk` → `.stack` of panes) size to content and **the canvas scrolls**. Do not give the last stack pane `flex: 1` / crush it — that creates a dead scrollport. `.stack.flow` is an alias of the same stack behaviour.
- Table: `.data` inside `.sheet`. Text and status align to the start. Numeric columns use `class="num"` on the header and the cell, values use `Money` when they are money, and the figures are tabular. Phone numbers, logins, and other Latin identifiers stay in `<bdi dir="ltr">`. The operations header and cell use `class="row-actions"`, centered with the trigger. Do not reuse `.ops` on a table cell; that class is a flex row and pulls the cell out of the table. Do not clip names or amounts.
- Line operations: immediate actions are rows in `.command-list`. Forms that need a value stay in `.command-forms`, one field and its button per row. Do not put those actions back into a card grid.
- Row actions: `RowMenu` from `components/row-menu.tsx` is the only per-row trigger. Pass a label that names the record. Destructive items use `danger` and an icon. Page-level actions, such as creating a record, stay visible. An inline price field keeps its own save control.
- Status: `<Badge variant={tone} dot>` (`components/ui/badge.tsx`) with a text label; the tone comes from `lib/status-tone.ts`.
- Dialog: `Dialog` from `components/dialog.tsx`. Sizes are `confirm`, `form` (default, about 600px), and `wide`. Put fields in the children and actions in `footer` (`secondary` cancel, `primary` save). Permission lists use `.perm-grid`. A dialog with several independent operations uses `.op-blocks` and keeps destructive actions in the footer. Checkboxes use `label.check`; do not give them text-field dimensions. Do not build a second overlay.
- Empty: `.empty` inside the pane. It already has 14px padding; never add `style={{ padding }}`.

Tokens stay `--rd-*` in `app/styles/tokens.css`. Arabic and Latin text stays Noto Kufi Arabic, Hebrew stays IBM Plex Sans Hebrew, and numbers use `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` on the same font. No new font and no raw hex.
